msgctxt "#30075"
msgid "Title Manager"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30076"
msgid "Install and uninstall games, title updates and DLC in saves/Cemu/mlc01, the emulated console's storage, and convert the loaded title to a .wua."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30077"
msgid "Install Games"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30078"
msgid "Installs every game from the source directory (system/Cemu/titles), subfolders included, into the emulated Wii U's installed game directory (saves/Cemu/mlc01/usr/title/00050000), as the console installs a game from its disc. A game is a disc image (.wud, .wux, .iso) or a .wua; the title update and DLC a .wua holds are installed with it. An encrypted disc image (.wud, .wux) needs its disc key: in a file beside it with the same name and the extension .key (game.wux, game.key), or in system/Cemu/keys.txt. A game already installed in the same or a newer version is left alone.\n\nWhen this is ON, installing begins immediately, with its progress shown as a notification, and it turns OFF again when all games are installed and this menu is exited or another option is changed. An installed game is started by loading the .rpx in its code folder in the installed game directory; its disc image is not needed any more."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30079"
msgid "Uninstall Game"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30080"
msgid "Uninstalls the running game and all associated title updates and DLC from the installed directory (saves/Cemu/mlc01/usr/title) once the game is closed or reset; the option stays ON until then. Saves for the game's title ID (saves/Cemu/mlc01/usr/save/<title id>) are not removed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30081"
msgid "Install Content"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30082"
msgid "Installs every title update and DLC from the source directory (system/Cemu/titles), subfolders included, into the installed directory (saves/Cemu/mlc01/usr/title). Each one goes in a folder of its own in the source directory; a NUS download (.app files) needs its title.tmd and its title.tik, the decryption key, next to them. A version already installed that is the same or newer is left alone.\n\nWhen this is ON, installing begins immediately, with its progress shown as a notification, and it turns OFF again when all content is installed and this menu is exited or another option is changed. The game uses the installed content once it is restarted.\n\nContent from other locations can be installed with RetroArch's Main Menu > Load Content, by selecting the corresponding title.tmd, with its title.tik beside it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30083"
msgid "Uninstall Content"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30084"
msgid "Uninstalls the running game's title update and DLC from the installed directory (saves/Cemu/mlc01/usr/title) once the game is closed or reset; the option stays ON until then. Copies in the source directory (system/Cemu/titles) are left alone."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30085"
msgid "Remove Files After Installing"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30086"
msgid "Removes what Install Games and Install Content have installed from the source directory (system/Cemu/titles): a title update's or DLC's folder once it is installed, and a disc image (with its .key file) or .wua once everything it holds is installed. Files the running game uses are removed when it is closed or reset.\n\nWARNING: this permanently removes files from the source directory. That directory is for the core to manage; keep game data you want to archive elsewhere."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30087"
msgid "Core"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30088"
msgid "Options of this core that standalone Cemu does not have."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30089"
msgid "Internal Resolution (Restart)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30090"
msgid "A generic fallback for games without a resolution graphic pack: resizes every screen-shaped render target, which some games use for things that break when resized. A multiple of the game's own resolution: for a 720p game 0.5x is 640x360, a quarter of the pixels, and 2x is 2560x1440; for a 1080p game 0.5x is 960x540. When a resolution pack is enabled for the loaded game (Graphic Packs), the pack sets the resolution."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30091"
msgid "0.25x (320x180 at 720p)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30092"
msgid "0.5x (640x360 at 720p)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30093"
msgid "0.75x (960x540 at 720p)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30094"
msgid "Native"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30095"
msgid "1.5x (1920x1080 at 720p)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30096"
msgid "2x (2560x1440 at 720p)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30097"
msgid "3x (3840x2160 at 720p)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30098"
msgid "Render Ahead One Frame"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30099"
msgid "Lets Cemu start drawing the next frame while RetroArch shows the last one, as standalone Cemu does. Smoother where frames take most of the frame time to draw, with one frame more input latency."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30100"
msgid "Audio Thread (Restart)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30101"
msgid "On: RetroArch takes the audio on its own thread, and the Wii U's audio runs by the clock as in standalone Cemu, so it does not break up while a frame is late (loading, shader compilation). RetroArch's Audio Sync then no longer paces the frames; Vertical Sync does, and RetroArch's audio statistics stay empty. Off: the audio is handed over with each frame."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30102"
msgid "Reduce BC1 Texture Memory (Restart)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30103"
msgid "Halves what BC1 textures cost on a GPU that cannot sample BC, at the price of one bit of green. No effect where BC is supported."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30104"
msgid "Show Game FPS"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30105"
msgid "Shows the frame rate the game renders at on RetroArch's on-screen display, once a second."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30106"
msgid "Logging"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30107"
msgid "Extra log output, for diagnosing problems."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30108"
msgid "Write Cemu Log to log.txt"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30109"
msgid "Log File Access (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30110"
msgid "Log Thread Synchronisation (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30111"
msgid "Log System API Calls (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30112"
msgid "Log Texture Memory (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30113"
msgid "Reports how much of the texture memory is BC that had to be decompressed because this GPU cannot sample it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30114"
msgid "Log Controller API Calls (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30115"
msgid "Logs every controller call a title makes - which pads it probed for and what it was told. Noisy; for a few seconds at a time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30116"
msgid "Log Audio and Frame Pacing (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30117"
msgid "Once a second, how many samples AX produced, how many the ring had to drop, and how many the frontend took; and how many times the frontend ran the core, how many frames the title finished, and where the time went (waiting for the GPU thread, presenting, audio). For working out whether a slow game is held up by the emulated CPU, the GPU or the frontend."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30118"
msgid "Log Thread CPU Time (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30119"
msgid "Once a second, how busy each emulated PowerPC core's thread, the GPU thread and the frontend's thread were, as a share of one host core. A thread near 100% is the one a slow game is waiting on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30120"
msgid "Dump Shaders (debugging)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30121"
msgid "Writes the source of every shader the game uses to system/Cemu/dump/shaders, named by its hashes as they appear in log.txt. For reporting a shader that fails or draws wrongly on a particular GPU. Slows shader compilation down and fills the folder quickly, so turn it off again afterwards."
msgstr ""
